  📋 SIGNAL - "RSI Divergence + Long Entry" (Weekly bars). Fires on the EXACT
  entry candle: the latest week bar is the first confirmation close.

  1) LOWER LOW: L2 = a new low 1-2 weeks before the latest bar
     (lowest low of 12 weeks), LOWER than an earlier swing low L1
     (3-30 weeks before it; lower than 2 bars each side).
  2) RSI HIGHER LOW: RSI(14) at L2 > RSI at L1, and RSI at L1 <= 40.
  3) CONFIRMATION CLOSE = ENTRY: the latest bar is green, closes above the
     previous close and in the upper half of its range, it is the FIRST such
     candle since L2, and nothing traded below L2 since.

  📋 OUTPUT
  Entry_Price = the confirmation close (Entry_Date)
  Stop_Loss   = L2 - 0.1 ATR(14)  (below the lower low)
  Target      = previous swing high (highest high of 20 weeks up to L1)
  Reward_R    = (Target - Entry) / (Entry - Stop)
  Swing_Low_Date / Prior_Swing_Low_Date = L2 / L1

  📋 SCORE (0-100)
  25 base + RSI divergence (0-25) + depth of the lower low (0-15)
  + Reward_R (0-20) + how oversold L1 was (0-15)
